{
  "entity0": {
    "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or Integrator feedback yet. The contract gives no evidence to tune against, so I am choosing a conservative, symmetric baseline. Five line sensors spaced 20 mm apart at x = -0.04 to +0.04 cover 0.08 m sideways, about three times the 25 mm tape width. That keeps the line visible through moderate offsets and gives the signal a usable slope. The sensors sit 50 mm ahead of the axle, so the controller sees the line before the wheels reach it, which reduces phase lag at speed. Sensor footprints are 12 mm, which is smaller than the tape, so readings are sharp at the edges and the signal responds quickly. Weights are antisymmetric (-2, -1, 0, 1, 2) to match the sensor layout, so the steering signal is zero on the centre line and scales with offset. Wheel track is 0.12 m and body width 0.12 m. The off-track limit is then max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.03) = 0.06 m, a comfortable margin for the robot to recover. Mass is 0.8 kg, mid-range, and the body is 0.18 m long. Expected result: a stable baseline that completes the oval and s-bend tracks, with the main risks being sharp slalom bends and the speed needed to finish in 3 s. Those are the things to measure first.",
    "geometry": {
      "sensor_positions": [
        {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
        {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05}
      ],
      "sensor_size": 0.012,
      "wheel_track": 0.12,
      "wheel_radius": 0.03,
      "body_width": 0.12,
      "body_length": 0.18,
      "mass": 0.8
    },
    "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array, 20 mm spacing, 50 mm ahead of the axle, with antisymmetric weights so signal is zero on centre and grows with offset. Moderate wheel and mass values, keeping the off-track margin at 0.06 m. Purpose: get a clean first race and a first set of measurements to see whether the array's width, forward position, or footprint size is limiting. Expect completion on the oval and s-bend; slalom is the likely failure point.",
    "feedback_request": {
      "requested_from": "Robot Integrator",
      "questions": [
        "Is the 5-sensor, 20 mm spacing array sufficient for a stable signal, or is there dead zone or saturation at the outer sensors?",
        "Does the 50 mm forward offset cause lag or overshoot at high base_speed?",
        "Which geometry parameter (sensor width, spacing, forward position, wheel_track, mass) most limits achievable speed without losing the line?",
        "Is the signal sensitive to noise at the outer sensors, given the 12 mm footprint?"
      ],
      "return_format": "Short notes plus the single geometry change you would make first and why."
    },
    "learning": "No evidence yet. The baseline is chosen for interpretability: symmetric, moderate, and with a known off-track margin. Next iteration, adjust the array width and forward position based on the first race's rms_error, max_error and line_loss_events, and adjust mass or wheel_track based on completion_time and steering_oscillation.",
    "_presentation_note": ""
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor array",
      "notes": "Symmetric five-sensor baseline with 20 mm spacing, 50 mm ahead of the axle, antisymmetric weights, and moderate body and mass. No race data exists yet, so this is a conservative starting point. Next iteration should tune array width and forward position from the first race's rms_error and line_loss_events."
    }
  }
}
